1
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:13,500
Love, Lust, Art and Religion

2
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Sirens is a comedy, drama film directed by John Duigan.

3
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:28,500
In 1930s Australia, Anglican clergyman Anthony Campion and his prim wife, Estella, are asked to visit noted painter
Norman Lindsay, whose planned contribution to an international art exhibit is considered blasphemous.

4
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:36,000
While Campion and Lindsay debate, Estella finds herself drawn to the three beautiful models sitting
for the painter's current work, freethinking Sheela, sensual Pru and virginal Giddy.

5
00:30:37,500 --> 00:30:43,500
Anthony Campion, played by Hugh Grant.

6
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Estella Campion, played by Tara Fitzgerald.

7
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:58,500
Norman Lindsay, played by Sam Neill.

8
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Sheela, played by Elle Macpherson.

9
00:55:07,500 --> 00:55:13,500
Giddy, played by Portia De Rossi.

10
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
Pru, played by Kate Fischer.

11
01:07:22,500 --> 01:07:28,500
Sirens is a 1994 film, based on the life of artist and author Norman Lindsay, written and
directed by John Duigan and set in Australia during the interwar period.

12
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Sirens was mostly filmed at the Norman Lindsay Gallery and Museum, Lindsay's home and
studio in Faulconbridge, New South Wales and the town of Sofala near Bathurst.

13
01:19:37,500 --> 01:19:43,500
Sirens, Four Weddings and a Funeral and Bitter Moon—all released in the US within weeks of one
another—were the films that brought Hugh Grant to the attention of American audiences.

14
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:51,000
The film explores themes of married couple, pastor,
painting, seduction, drawing and painting.

15
01:31:52,500 --> 01:31:58,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
